  "query_preview": "(Today through Sunday)...\nIssued at 258 AM EDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nEarly This Morning...\n\nThe surface front has moved south of central Indiana, but a couple \nof upper impulses along with a surface wave riding along the front \nare bringing enough forcing for numerous showers and some \nthunderstorms to move into the area. \n\nThis forcing will continue through the predawn hours, so have gone \nwith higher PoPs over much of the area. For much of the area, CAPE \nis elevated with an inversion closer to the surface. Will have to \nwatch the far south where better instability remains closer to the \nsurface, but odds for any severe weather remain low. Heavy rain and \nlocalized flooding will be the threats as some training of cells may \noccur.\n\nToday and Tonight...\n\nAt 12Z, rain from one of the upper impulses will likely still be \nongoing for parts of the area. Will go likely PoPs for portions of \nthe east and southeast early in the period. Some of the latest \nhourly guidance is showing another upper impulse generating more \nnumerous showers moving west to east during the morning. Not \nconfident enough yet to up PoPs elsewhere at this time, but will \nkeep an eye on how things develop.\n\nOtherwise, chances for rain will diminish during the day as overall \nforcing exits. Will have most areas dry by 21Z.\n\nMoisture will be trapped below an inversion so will keep skies \nmostly cloudy. With the clouds and cooler air behind the front, \nhighs will only reach the middle 60s far northeast to near 80 far \nsouthwest.\n\nClouds will continue to hang around tonight. Lows will be in the 50s.\n\nTuesday and Wednesday...\n\nA weakening upper low will approach the area on Tuesday. Forcing \nwill be weak, so for now have not gone with any mentionable PoPs. \nHowever, wouldn't be surprised to see some isolated showers develop \nduring the afternoon.\n\nThe upper low will be east of the area on Wednesday. Most forcing \nwill be east of the area, but an isolated shower is possible in the \nextreme east during the afternoon.\n\nLingering moisture will keep skies mostly cloudy on Tuesday, with \nwestern areas seeing some partial clearing on Wednesday. Highs will \ngenerally be in the upper 60s to middle 70s.\n\nThursday and beyond...\n\nSurface high pressure will keep the weather quiet during this \nperiod. Temperatures will remain below normal into the first part of \nthe weekend, then readings may return to above normal (highs around \n80) by next Monday.",
